WEBVTT

00:00.507 --> 00:03.134
YOU ARE HERE

00:03.844 --> 00:04.845
Koichi…

00:07.848 --> 00:09.099
I'm over here, Koichi.

00:09.307 --> 00:11.809
Ah! R-Rohan Kishibe!

00:11.893 --> 00:14.520
Hey, hey. Don't be so defensive.

00:14.855 --> 00:17.399
My days of harming you are over.

00:17.482 --> 00:20.443
Besides, reading your history
with Heaven's Door

00:20.527 --> 00:24.072
filled me with
a sense of respect for you.

00:24.239 --> 00:26.908
It's as if we're two peas in a pod.

00:27.117 --> 00:28.243
Wouldn't you agree?

00:29.077 --> 00:30.286
Uh…

00:30.495 --> 00:33.414
So, I'd like to ask you
a little question.

00:33.665 --> 00:37.960
You see, until I was about four,
I called this area home.

00:38.170 --> 00:40.630
And I've been looking
for my old place.

00:41.173 --> 00:43.300
You could call it nostalgia,
if you will.

00:43.592 --> 00:46.428
Recalling childhood is central
to a manga artist's work.

00:46.928 --> 00:49.805
But they're memories
of a three-to-four-year-old.

00:49.890 --> 00:51.308
It's all a bit foggy.

00:51.433 --> 00:52.183
Oh…

00:52.809 --> 00:56.145
My question is about this town map.

00:56.313 --> 00:57.814
It's really quite peculiar.

00:57.814 --> 01:02.314
CONVENIENCE STORE OWSON
KISARA DRUGSTORE
SOBA SHOP ARISUGAWA
TAILOR TANAKA

00:58.064 --> 00:58.814
Ponder this.

00:58.940 --> 01:00.399
Here you can see
the Soba Shop Arisugawa,

01:00.483 --> 01:01.984
Kisara Drugstore,

01:02.068 --> 01:05.676
and the Owson convenience store
situated right-to-left.

01:05.864 --> 01:06.656
Huh?

01:06.781 --> 01:08.783
Now look at
the physical shops themselves.

01:08.950 --> 01:11.118
From the right, you can see
the Soba Shop Arisugawa,

01:11.203 --> 01:14.331
Kisara Drugstore, and…

01:15.290 --> 01:17.417
Owson on the left…

01:17.709 --> 01:18.876
Huh?

01:18.960 --> 01:23.089
The map shows no road between
the Owson and the drugstore.

01:23.173 --> 01:24.465
How sloppy…

01:24.591 --> 01:27.093
Koichi, will you tag along?

01:27.344 --> 01:29.846
I would be forever in your debt
if you could show me around.

01:29.971 --> 01:33.474
Huh? Well, I, uh…

01:34.017 --> 01:35.643
And here I, Rohan Kishibe,

01:35.727 --> 01:37.520
went the extra mile
to ask with the utmost courtesy.

01:38.438 --> 01:39.313
I see.

01:39.439 --> 01:42.942
So you can't bring yourself
to show me around for a few meters.

01:43.193 --> 01:46.070
He sure is self-centered. Jeez…

01:46.154 --> 01:47.780
I have five minutes, okay, Sensei?

01:48.114 --> 01:49.323
Just five minutes!

01:56.623 --> 02:01.044
EPISODE 17
ROHAN KISHIBE'S ADVENTURE

01:57.499 --> 01:58.791
Strange isn't it?

01:58.875 --> 02:01.065
Even my official Shoin Press
1/3000-scale map of Morioh

02:01.419 --> 02:04.797
makes absolutely no mention
of this street.

02:04.881 --> 02:07.008
Huh? Sometimes if you find
a map error,

02:07.092 --> 02:09.052
you can get
a bookstore gift certificate.

02:16.685 --> 02:17.894
Ugh…

02:18.353 --> 02:21.064
Blast it, this map is hopeless.

02:21.147 --> 02:22.398
Look, Koichi.

02:22.232 --> 02:25.944
YONEMORI

02:22.482 --> 02:23.691
This map doesn't call out

02:23.199 --> 02:25.944
HONMA

02:23.775 --> 02:25.902
the "Yonemori," "Honma,"
or "Onodera" residence either.

02:23.952 --> 02:25.944
ONODERA

02:24.705 --> 02:25.944
NUMAKURA

02:26.027 --> 02:27.611
This map is riddled
with oversights.

02:27.696 --> 02:29.447
They're going to owe me
a lot more than

02:29.531 --> 02:30.782
two or three gift certificates.

02:31.074 --> 02:32.116
Rohan-sensei..

02:32.367 --> 02:34.660
The place looks abandoned.

02:35.453 --> 02:37.246
ROCKY

02:37.998 --> 02:39.958
What a weird area.

02:40.250 --> 02:43.586
The five or so houses around here
look completely unoccupied.

02:43.712 --> 02:46.339
Even the vending machines are off.

02:47.507 --> 02:48.257
Huh?

02:48.341 --> 02:49.759
That mailbox…

02:49.843 --> 02:53.263
We made our first turn
at this corner.

02:56.308 --> 02:57.434
Too weird…

02:57.642 --> 03:00.603
We're right back where we started.

03:00.895 --> 03:03.939
<i>But we turned right,
left, then right…</i>

03:04.691 --> 03:08.277
Someone could be attacking us
with their Stand.

03:08.445 --> 03:09.529
Huh? Stand?!

03:10.071 --> 03:13.199
Koichi, do me a favor and deploy
Reverb into the sky above us.

03:13.867 --> 03:14.951
Of course!

03:15.035 --> 03:17.078
From above, it'll know
exactly where we need to go.

03:17.162 --> 03:18.580
Reverb Act 1!

03:24.252 --> 03:25.253
What's wrong?

03:25.837 --> 03:27.797
Something was up there.

03:27.964 --> 03:30.925
Something grazed Reverb.

03:31.426 --> 03:33.302
I couldn't see anything.

03:33.553 --> 03:35.972
I know something
came in contact with Reverb!

03:36.264 --> 03:38.599
Are you two lost?

03:42.979 --> 03:44.897
I'd be happy to be your guide.

03:44.981 --> 03:45.731
A girl!

03:45.982 --> 03:48.067
That girl's a Stand user!

03:49.402 --> 03:50.820
Heaven's Door!

03:52.364 --> 03:53.865
Without further ado…

03:53.948 --> 03:55.491
I shall seize victory, post haste!

03:56.409 --> 03:57.159
BOOM

04:01.748 --> 04:03.166
We should be safe now.

04:03.249 --> 04:06.710
She won't be able to harm us.

04:06.795 --> 04:07.629
Amazing!

04:08.213 --> 04:10.840
I-It's like you launched
your drawing into mid air…

04:11.049 --> 04:13.468
I suppose I've made some progress.

04:13.551 --> 04:16.595
Though it doesn't work on artless

04:16.679 --> 04:18.597
Rohan-manga haters like Josuke.

04:19.099 --> 04:21.017
She and I are on
the same wavelength.

04:22.310 --> 04:25.563
She's not a Stand user.
She's an ordinary girl.

04:25.647 --> 04:27.815
Huh? So she's not out to get us?

04:27.982 --> 04:30.859
Correct. Nothing can
hide from Heaven's Door.

04:31.528 --> 04:34.280
Her name is Reimi Sugimoto,
aged 16.

04:34.406 --> 04:36.783
Her address is 3-12,
Kotodai, Morioh.

04:36.991 --> 04:37.992
That's not far from here.

04:38.451 --> 04:39.618
She has no boyfriend.

04:39.702 --> 04:43.038
Her bust/waist/hip are
82-57-84 centimeters.

04:43.206 --> 04:44.874
Beside her left nipple
is a single mole.

04:45.333 --> 04:47.543
She had her first period
the month of September, age 11.

04:47.669 --> 04:49.587
Her first time kissing a boy,

04:49.671 --> 04:50.755
he rammed his tongue
down her throat.

04:50.839 --> 04:53.091
Just a minute, Rohan Kishibe!

04:53.174 --> 04:55.467
If that girl's not a Stand user,

04:55.593 --> 04:57.761
then I refuse to allow you
to read any further!

04:57.846 --> 04:59.889
All right, all right.

05:00.265 --> 05:01.557
Simmer down.

05:01.683 --> 05:05.186
"I will forget everything
that just happened." There.

05:07.021 --> 05:08.605
I'd be happy to be your guide.

05:09.232 --> 05:11.609
This area trips up a lot of people.

05:11.860 --> 05:13.736
A lot of these alleys
look the same.

05:13.862 --> 05:15.113
Please point us
in the right direction

05:15.196 --> 05:16.322
and we'll be on our way.

05:16.739 --> 05:19.491
Absolutely not.
Simple explanation won't cut it.

05:19.576 --> 05:21.536
I'll be your guide. Follow me.

05:25.540 --> 05:26.290
Want one?

05:26.958 --> 05:28.000
You sure?

05:28.126 --> 05:30.628
Then go ahead and grab that end.

05:31.921 --> 05:32.671
SNAP

05:32.505 --> 05:32.693
Uh-oh, some girl's gonna dump you.

05:37.051 --> 05:38.635
Who is this girl?

05:38.970 --> 05:40.262
It's Pocky fortune-telling.

05:40.430 --> 05:41.931
The break gives me insight
into you and your future.

05:42.557 --> 05:44.225
Well, you are self-centered, right?

05:44.350 --> 05:46.810
And you tend to push
people's buttons.

05:47.061 --> 05:48.479
That's why you'll get dumped.

05:48.771 --> 05:52.524
Hear that, Koichi?
Now we know she's totally off base!

05:52.692 --> 05:54.402
Me, self-centered?!

05:54.652 --> 05:56.987
Well, two can play at this game.

05:57.238 --> 06:00.699
Light pink nail polish
means you're afraid of love.

06:00.867 --> 06:01.659
When push comes to shove,

06:01.743 --> 06:02.994
you let love
slip through your fingers.

06:03.244 --> 06:03.994
Huh?

06:05.288 --> 06:06.622
No way…

06:07.040 --> 06:09.834
This isn't so much fortune-telling
as it is psychological prodding.

06:09.918 --> 06:13.379
Regardless of love,
something else unnerves you.

06:25.141 --> 06:26.308
It's said this house…

06:27.060 --> 06:30.271
was the scene of
a murder fifteen years ago.

06:30.355 --> 06:32.273
A murder?!

06:32.899 --> 06:33.983
Murder…

06:34.400 --> 06:36.485
No one lives there now.

06:38.321 --> 06:40.197
Do you wish to hear the story?

06:41.950 --> 06:45.203
The old lady next door
once told me.

06:45.620 --> 06:47.371
The day it happened,
at the dead of night,

06:47.830 --> 06:50.374
while the young girl
was asleep in her bedroom,

06:50.792 --> 06:55.292
she awoke to a strange dripping
coming from her parents' room.

06:58.800 --> 07:02.386
The sound puzzled the girl,
who then called out to her parents,

07:02.637 --> 07:04.388
but there was no reply.

07:04.681 --> 07:08.184
But the girl wasn't
particularly scared, because…

07:08.476 --> 07:10.311
She was accompanied
by her trusty dog.

07:10.853 --> 07:11.603
Trusty dog?

07:11.813 --> 07:13.856
Yes. He was a great big guard dog.

07:13.982 --> 07:17.819
In the pitch-dark, she would offer
her hand to him under the bed,

07:18.111 --> 07:19.862
and there was always
a whimper and a lick.

07:20.029 --> 07:22.281
Arnold was her reassurance.

07:23.157 --> 07:27.657
But the dripping continued
for several minutes…

07:29.956 --> 07:34.126
Finally, her curiosity
got the best of her.

07:34.210 --> 07:35.711
She investigated, then…

07:39.465 --> 07:41.592
There was Arnold, throat slashed,

07:41.676 --> 07:43.803
and hanging from the coat rack.

07:44.178 --> 07:47.556
And there was his blood dripping,
PLIP-plop.

07:49.058 --> 07:51.393
Then, suddenly, there was
a voice from under the bed.

07:51.561 --> 07:55.690
"Your hand is so sweet and tender,
Sweetheart. Whimper, whimper…"

07:56.691 --> 07:59.652
"I already murdered
Mommy and Daddy." And then…

07:59.777 --> 08:02.154
He murdered the girl, too!

08:03.448 --> 08:05.741
I-Is that a true story?!

08:07.327 --> 08:09.495
Sounded real, huh?

08:09.579 --> 08:11.080
That's for that nail-polish
wisecrack.

08:13.082 --> 08:14.249
Whew…

08:14.459 --> 08:17.962
My heart can't take
stuff like that… Jeez…

08:21.591 --> 08:22.633
DRIP

08:30.767 --> 08:31.642
Wha—

08:32.018 --> 08:32.810
That's…

08:33.227 --> 08:37.064
Yes… That girl was me.

08:37.148 --> 08:39.650
We're ghosts. Both Arnold and I.

08:43.988 --> 08:46.073
<i>G-Ghosts?</i>

08:46.574 --> 08:51.036
<i>Heaven's Door read only
her living memories.</i>

08:51.120 --> 08:52.454
<i>I had no idea.</i>

08:53.081 --> 08:57.581
You two've entered the area
where I died fifteen years ago.

08:58.920 --> 09:00.755
I guess we're on
the same wavelength.

09:01.297 --> 09:04.258
This is the gateway
between the living and the dead.

09:08.888 --> 09:11.640
REVERB

09:13.142 --> 09:14.476
Run, Koichi!

09:31.160 --> 09:32.536
I-It's no use!

09:32.620 --> 09:34.455
Summon Reverb, Koichi!

09:34.539 --> 09:36.582
It can show us the way from above!

09:36.708 --> 09:39.627
She must've been the one who
made contact with Reverb up there.

09:39.711 --> 09:41.421
Never mind,
just get him up there, Koichi!

09:44.716 --> 09:45.299
Wha—

09:45.383 --> 09:48.010
What?! A wall appeared in the sky!

09:48.136 --> 09:51.472
K-Koichi, that's the ground.

09:51.848 --> 09:53.432
Huh?! Ah, what?!

09:54.183 --> 09:56.852
Y-You're the one in the air.

09:58.646 --> 10:02.524
There's only one way
out of this place.

10:03.359 --> 10:05.069
And I know where it is.

10:05.903 --> 10:08.280
H-How the heck
do you fight a ghost?

10:08.364 --> 10:10.240
Please don't possess us!

10:10.491 --> 10:11.450
Hold your horses.

10:11.701 --> 10:13.619
Stop treating me
like some kind of vengeful spirit.

10:13.703 --> 10:15.538
What did I do to you?

10:15.621 --> 10:18.206
You've done a fine job
of scaring yourselves!

10:19.292 --> 10:21.002
I didn't trap you guys here.

10:21.335 --> 10:24.004
We're standing between the world
of the living and the dead.

10:24.422 --> 10:27.758
You two hold some kind
of strange power, don't you?

10:27.967 --> 10:29.760
They're called Stands?

10:30.052 --> 10:32.054
Maybe that's what
got you mixed up in all this.

10:32.513 --> 10:34.556
So you're not against us?

10:35.016 --> 10:37.226
You really are suspicious,
aren't you?

10:37.685 --> 10:39.311
I guess I'm proof
of that Stone Tape theory.

10:39.771 --> 10:43.065
Once a ghost,
I became bound to this place.

10:43.566 --> 10:45.109
Here, for fifteen years,

10:45.193 --> 10:46.652
I've pleaded with
passersby to listen.

10:46.736 --> 10:48.154
To let me share my story.

10:48.821 --> 10:53.321
But you two are
the first people to really listen.

10:54.327 --> 10:56.203
I told you I'd help you
get out of here,

10:56.287 --> 10:57.621
so that's what I'll do.

10:58.039 --> 10:59.665
After I finish the story, that is.

11:00.166 --> 11:00.958
Story?

11:01.667 --> 11:02.793
As I was saying…

11:02.877 --> 11:05.713
Before I could see
the murderer's face,

11:06.005 --> 11:08.090
I was stabbed in the back.

11:08.549 --> 11:09.967
It was late and very dark,

11:10.218 --> 11:11.886
and I was desperately trying
to get away.

11:13.095 --> 11:15.722
The murderer is still loose.

11:16.974 --> 11:19.101
He's somewhere here in Morioh.

11:20.686 --> 11:22.562
That's what I wanted to say.

11:22.855 --> 11:25.607
He's assimilated into
Morioh society.

11:26.609 --> 11:29.320
Wait. Are you telling us because…

11:29.695 --> 11:31.405
I'm not asking you to catch him.

11:31.739 --> 11:33.866
But I want you to tell someone…

11:34.492 --> 11:37.703
Tell the police…
Anyone who can catch him…

11:37.787 --> 11:41.624
Hey, why should that be
our responsibility?

11:41.791 --> 11:43.167
Rohan-sensei!

11:43.501 --> 11:46.170
It's all right.
I'm trying to remain level-headed.

11:46.671 --> 11:49.632
I'm sorry your life
was cut tragically short…

11:50.341 --> 11:53.969
Still, why must we
find the murderer to appease

11:54.095 --> 11:55.971
your feelings of resentment?

11:56.806 --> 11:58.474
Letting go of this world,

11:58.724 --> 12:00.976
and moving onto the next

12:01.060 --> 12:03.812
would be a much more fitting
existence for a ghost.

12:05.648 --> 12:07.858
Do you have any idea
how many boys and girls

12:07.942 --> 12:10.110
have gone missing from this town?

12:10.194 --> 12:11.195
Huh? No.

12:12.613 --> 12:14.781
It's eight times
the national average.

12:16.450 --> 12:20.287
And some of them
are being slaughtered in silence.

12:20.997 --> 12:22.164
By him.

12:22.248 --> 12:23.791
W-Wait a second!

12:24.125 --> 12:26.293
You mean these murders
are still happening?

12:26.627 --> 12:28.879
Hey! You can't
throw around allegations!

12:29.130 --> 12:31.173
You said you didn't even catch
a glimpse of the murderer's face!

12:31.549 --> 12:32.675
How would you know that?

12:33.050 --> 12:37.550
The souls of those
murdered dominate these skies!

12:39.473 --> 12:41.600
Their wounds are just like mine.

12:42.977 --> 12:45.896
It's horrifying…
Such a deep gash…

12:46.230 --> 12:48.065
I can't communicate
with those souls

12:48.149 --> 12:49.817
making their way to the Other Side,

12:49.901 --> 12:51.152
but over and over I witness them.

12:51.319 --> 12:54.697
I know his obsession! I know!

12:55.239 --> 12:57.282
Morioh,
my birthplace, my hometown,

12:57.658 --> 13:00.243
has for fifteen years
stood in the shadow of murder.

13:00.578 --> 13:05.078
It's terrifying,
and it's humiliating.

13:05.833 --> 13:09.211
When they catch him,
my cherished Morioh

13:09.503 --> 13:13.507
will be known across
Japan as that butcher's town.

13:14.550 --> 13:18.178
But it doesn't change that
we must stop him as fast as we can!

13:18.846 --> 13:21.056
He's preying on someone
as we speak,

13:21.140 --> 13:22.766
and there's nothing I can do.

13:23.351 --> 13:25.561
Who will he kill next?

13:27.730 --> 13:29.773
If you and your beating hearts

13:29.857 --> 13:32.276
won't take back Morioh's
peace and dignity,

13:32.360 --> 13:34.862
then I'd like to know who will?!

13:38.282 --> 13:40.742
I hope you took in what I said…

13:41.452 --> 13:42.578
I have nothing more to say.

13:45.998 --> 13:49.918
I did. I'm shocked.

13:50.878 --> 13:53.088
I know… we have to do something.

13:53.547 --> 13:56.007
Hmph. I wouldn't be
too big-hearted, Koichi.

13:56.801 --> 13:58.177
It all spells trouble.

14:04.350 --> 14:08.145
But the murderer could
be a good source of inspiration.

14:08.562 --> 14:11.314
It might make for
some interesting manga!

14:13.985 --> 14:15.820
Can we get out this way?

14:17.613 --> 14:20.949
If you think he's good at heart…
Well, don't.

14:21.283 --> 14:22.617
And when it comes to
trustworthiness,

14:22.702 --> 14:24.078
he's shady at best.

14:24.203 --> 14:26.288
Hey, are you listening?

14:27.999 --> 14:30.835
All right. I'll show you
how to get to the exit.

14:31.210 --> 14:33.629
Huh? The exit? Where? Where is it?

14:34.922 --> 14:37.466
If you go past the mail box
and turn left, it's right there.

14:37.591 --> 14:38.592
Yes!

14:38.718 --> 14:39.593
Don't rush it!

14:39.760 --> 14:42.554
There's a rule
to making it through.

14:44.265 --> 14:45.099
A rule?

14:45.766 --> 14:47.601
Once you make your turn past
the mail box,

14:47.685 --> 14:50.312
you'll see the exit
about 20 meters away.

14:51.731 --> 14:55.943
No matter what happens,
promise me you'll never look back.

14:56.569 --> 14:58.487
Why? What for?

14:58.988 --> 15:01.156
It's the rule for passing
from this world to the next.

15:01.782 --> 15:04.326
Even Arnold understands that.

15:04.785 --> 15:09.080
Well, if a dog can handle it,
I guess I can too.

15:09.457 --> 15:11.584
And if we look back?

15:12.168 --> 15:15.838
Your souls will be dragged into
the next world.

15:16.172 --> 15:17.756
Death will take hold.

15:20.301 --> 15:21.552
Don't be scared!

15:21.635 --> 15:24.512
Just keep looking forward.
Simple, right?

15:33.856 --> 15:36.024
When we passed the mail box…

15:36.192 --> 15:40.070
Something flew past
our legs and went behind us!

15:40.321 --> 15:41.989
Remember, you mustn't look back!

15:42.281 --> 15:44.032
Just stay calm and collected.

15:49.830 --> 15:54.330
R-Rohan-sensei,
something's creeping up behind us.

15:55.086 --> 15:55.878
I know.

15:59.548 --> 16:00.757
<i>Something's there…</i>

16:00.841 --> 16:04.261
<i>Something's right by my head!</i>

16:04.929 --> 16:06.055
Ignore it!

16:06.430 --> 16:08.932
Something will always
try to make you look back.

16:09.058 --> 16:11.143
As long as you
don't look back at it,

16:11.227 --> 16:14.521
it can't touch you.
Don't let it get to you.

16:15.189 --> 16:19.689
N-Now something warm
and runny is oozing down my neck…

16:21.570 --> 16:24.072
Almost there!
That light is the way out.

16:24.365 --> 16:25.115
- Huh?
- What?

16:25.449 --> 16:26.658
Th-The exit…

16:26.867 --> 16:28.702
I can't take it anymore!

16:28.953 --> 16:31.163
Rohan-sensei, let's run!

16:31.455 --> 16:32.289
Don't panic!

16:32.373 --> 16:33.999
It'll try to trip you.

16:38.045 --> 16:39.546
You're safe now.

16:39.964 --> 16:41.256
You made it.

16:41.549 --> 16:43.592
Now you can turn around.

16:46.053 --> 16:48.263
That was terrifying!
Thank goodness it's over!

16:48.389 --> 16:49.932
That was a lie, Koichi!

16:50.224 --> 16:52.434
That wasn't me who said that!

16:52.560 --> 16:53.394
Huh?

16:53.727 --> 16:54.477
Impossible…

16:54.603 --> 16:56.771
Not yet. You can't turn around yet.

16:57.064 --> 16:59.608
This didn't happen when
I was by myself.

16:59.900 --> 17:01.026
They didn't try to trick me!

17:06.740 --> 17:07.782
Koichi!

17:08.367 --> 17:09.576
I don't quite understand it,

17:09.660 --> 17:10.827
but no peeking
and we're through, right?

17:11.287 --> 17:13.580
You're lucky I'm with you, Koichi.

17:13.664 --> 17:15.123
Heaven's Door!

17:15.457 --> 17:17.959
You'll lose your ability to see,
then fly through the air.

17:18.294 --> 17:19.044
CRASH

17:19.587 --> 17:21.213
BOOM

17:23.507 --> 17:25.300
You can calm down, Koichi.

17:26.385 --> 17:28.470
I'll reinscribe your ability
to see shortly.

17:37.688 --> 17:41.149
The alley between the convenience
store and drugstore is gone.

17:41.567 --> 17:43.777
W-We're finally back…

17:45.654 --> 17:47.864
This is where we'll stay.

17:49.366 --> 17:51.076
Until he's apprehended.

17:51.952 --> 17:56.452
Arnold and I will finally look back
and return to Mom and Dad,

17:56.957 --> 17:59.668
when peace and dignity
once again returns to Morioh.

18:00.085 --> 18:01.961
Until that day, I cannot leave.

18:03.005 --> 18:05.340
If you ever want to talk,
about anything,

18:06.133 --> 18:07.759
don't hesitate to come back.

18:08.219 --> 18:09.678
I'll be here,

18:10.054 --> 18:12.139
Rohan darling, Mr. Koichi…

18:13.307 --> 18:14.933
From the bottom of my heart,

18:15.267 --> 18:17.018
thank you for listening
to my story.

18:21.440 --> 18:24.818
To think that girl
called me "Rohan darling."

18:25.527 --> 18:27.195
Fairly presumptious, if you ask me.

18:29.031 --> 18:32.200
But… Reimi Sugimoto, huh…

18:32.576 --> 18:35.704
That spirit's demeanor…
it's something to be respected.

18:37.164 --> 18:38.665
For fifteen years,

18:38.749 --> 18:42.377
she's been waging
a solitary fight for the living.

18:45.965 --> 18:47.049
FAMILY MASSACRE CASE
REMAINS MYSTERY

18:47.132 --> 18:48.591
SUGIMOTO FAMILY GRAVE

18:51.387 --> 18:52.638
SUGIMOTO
REIMI

18:53.180 --> 18:55.557
There! Sugimoto Reimi, age 16.

18:55.933 --> 18:58.393
Not that I doubted her,
but now I've got evidence.

18:58.602 --> 19:00.895
Ah, you wouldn't happen to be…

19:01.230 --> 19:04.024
Rohan Kishibe, the manga artist?

19:04.233 --> 19:06.902
SUGIMOTO FAMILY GRAVE

19:05.109 --> 19:06.652
Do I know you?

19:11.198 --> 19:14.868
Rohan, you were only four,

19:15.119 --> 19:17.746
It doesn't surprise me
you have no recollection.

19:19.456 --> 19:23.084
Your house was
very close to theirs.

19:23.460 --> 19:24.878
The night of the incident,

19:24.962 --> 19:29.462
urgent business took your parents
away for the evening…

19:30.676 --> 19:33.512
Your parents and
the Sugimotos were very close,

19:33.679 --> 19:36.640
so they left you
with them for a single night.

19:37.891 --> 19:42.391
That night, Rohan,
you stayed at the Sugimoto's house.

19:42.896 --> 19:45.106
You were the only one rescued.

19:46.025 --> 19:49.028
I was… there?

19:49.653 --> 19:51.863
Once in police custody,

19:52.156 --> 19:56.451
you repeated over
and over through the tears:

19:56.994 --> 20:00.664
"Auntie Reimi snuck me
out the window."

20:01.373 --> 20:05.873
Reimi saved you before
the murderer could find you.

20:09.631 --> 20:12.634
That little girl…
No wonder she acted so familiar.

20:14.428 --> 20:17.347
So Heaven's Door
gives me no insight

20:17.431 --> 20:21.476
into my distant memories
or personal fate.

20:23.687 --> 20:26.981
<i>If you ever find yourself
in the alley of this story,</i>

20:27.566 --> 20:30.610
<i>never, ever, look back.</i>

20:33.113 --> 20:35.073
MORIOH LANDMARK 6
"GHOST ALLEY"
HOW TO GET THERE: TAKE #11 BUS
FROM MORIOH STATION
TO KOTODAI SHOPPING DISTRICT.
THE ALLEY LIES BETWEEN
THE OWSON CONVENIENCE STORE
AND KISARA DRUGSTORE AT 2-CHOME.

20:35.157 --> 20:37.159
BEWARE: IF YOU ARE ONE OF THE FEW
WHO CAN SEE THE ALLEY AND
HAPPEN TO WANDER INTO ITS DEPTHS,
DO NOT LOOK BACK, NO MATTER WHAT.

20:37.618 --> 20:39.828
I really did meet a ghost!

20:39.912 --> 20:41.997
- The girl in that picture is Reimi!
- Okay, we get it.

20:42.122 --> 20:43.790
- So, I did a little research,
- I said I believe you.

20:43.999 --> 20:45.291
- And it turns out she was a student
- I said I believe you.

20:45.459 --> 20:47.043
- At Bodogaoka High School, too.
<i>- She's cute… Just my type.</i>

20:47.211 --> 20:49.254
<i>If only I'd been born
fifteen years earlier.</i>

20:49.463 --> 20:53.300
Eventually, we should
probably meet this ghost, too.

20:53.425 --> 20:57.387
You know, Koichi, if we tell Jotaro
or Mr. Joseph about any of this,

20:57.638 --> 21:00.182
you can bet
they'll have one question:

21:00.432 --> 21:03.685
"Is the murderer a Stand user?"

21:04.478 --> 21:07.189
W-Well… I don't know…

21:07.398 --> 21:10.442
Then it's up to the police
and judges.

21:10.567 --> 21:13.945
A murderer's loose in Morioh!

21:14.029 --> 21:18.199
I know. I'm saying Jotaro
and the Speedwagon Foundation

21:18.283 --> 21:21.577
won't just go after
some ordinary murderer.

21:22.329 --> 21:23.538
Try to relax.

21:23.664 --> 21:25.666
He's managed to completely evade
the all-powerful police

21:25.749 --> 21:27.208
for over a decade and a half.

21:27.709 --> 21:29.460
It's not like we'd
run into the guy,

21:29.545 --> 21:31.547
like grabbing some taxi
around here.

21:32.631 --> 21:35.508
Let's stay calm and
look into things carefully.

21:35.759 --> 21:38.219
So what'd 'ol Rohan have to say?

21:39.805 --> 21:41.973
Same as you, Josuke.

21:45.727 --> 21:47.019
Hey, be careful, Koichi.

21:47.104 --> 21:49.397
You gotta be alert
when you cross the road.

21:49.523 --> 21:51.775
S-Sorry…

22:02.202 --> 22:06.702
A long time ago, Morioh was
a summer escape for samurai.

22:07.666 --> 22:09.793
My ancestors were among them.

22:09.877 --> 22:12.129
But then it all went south
with my grandfather.

22:12.212 --> 22:14.964
All that's left is
the house I live in now.

22:15.048 --> 22:17.717
And of course
my miserable little office job.

22:19.720 --> 22:23.265
Hey, what happened to that nice
import watch I bought you?

22:23.724 --> 22:26.977
Ah, it's in your bag.
How could I forget?

22:27.394 --> 22:29.813
It was a little loose on you.

22:29.897 --> 22:31.356
Tomorrow we'll get it fixed.

22:41.742 --> 22:44.494
What's wrong? Why so coy?

22:45.746 --> 22:48.039
Now… Watch your step.

22:48.790 --> 22:52.627
Come, a magnificent weekend awaits.

22:54.046 --> 22:55.672
Just the two of us.

23:02.262 --> 23:04.180
You're dripping…

23:04.264 --> 23:06.599
Quite ill-mannered, I must say.

23:06.683 --> 23:08.351
I expect you to clean
that up yourself.

23:14.233 --> 23:18.733
I can't recall your name,
but no matter.

23:18.946 --> 23:21.990
Bravo. You tidied it up well.

23:22.908 --> 23:23.950
Now, then…

23:24.785 --> 23:26.703
You and I should make dinner.

23:27.621 --> 23:29.664
What, pray tell,
is your culinary strong suit?

23:32.459 --> 23:36.959
KIRA

23:39.258 --> 23:42.010
EPISODE 18
SHIGECHI'S HARVEST, PART 1
